// Settings → Interface → Auto-hide (#98), set by src/app/wiring/autohide.rs. Rust decides
// when the controls are awake (AppWindow.controls-visible); these say what hides when
// they are not, what keeps them shown, and how the bars animate.
export global AutoHide {
    in-out property <bool> top: true; // the top bar hides
    in-out property <bool> bottom: true; // the bottom bar hides
    in-out property <bool> cursor: true; // the mouse pointer hides over the video
    in-out property <bool> keep-panel: true; // an open panel, drawer or menu keeps them shown
    in-out property <bool> keep-hover: false; // the pointer over a bar keeps them shown
    in-out property <int> anim: 0; // 0 instant, 1 fade, 2 slide
}
